% Goal

One text-in / text-out call to a language model, reachable in the ways a local DJ app can legitimately use:

- Signed-in vendor CLI (the user's subscription; the vendor CLI owns its browser login): `claude-cli`, `codex-cli`, `grok-cli`.
- API key kept in the repository's gitignored `.env`: `anthropic-api` (ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, optional CLAWDJ_ANTHROPIC_MODEL, default `claude-opus-5-5`), `openai-api` (OPENAI_API_KEY + CLAWDJ_OPENAI_MODEL), `xai-api` (XAI_API_KEY + CLAWDJ_XAI_MODEL), `hcompany-api` (HAI_API_KEY, optional CLAWDJ_HCOMPANY_MODEL, default `holo3-1-35b-a3b`).
- Local llama.cpp `llama-server` (OpenAI-compatible; LLAMA_SERVER_URL, default http://127.0.0.1:8080).

% Requirements

1. `PROVIDERS` lists exactly the eight providers above with a human label, kind (`cli` | `api` | `local`), the one-time terminal sign-in command for CLI providers (`claude auth login`, `codex login`, `grok login --oauth`), and the env vars for API/local providers.
2. `status_all()` reports availability and a one-line human detail for every provider without raising: CLI installed and signed in; API key (and model where required) set; llama-server answering `/health`.
3. `ask()` sends one prompt and returns only the model's answer text. CLI providers run non-interactively with no tools, no web access and no persisted session; the prompt is passed on stdin or a temporary file, never in a shell string.
4. `.env` is loaded without overriding variables already set in the process environment.
5. The Anthropic API path uses the official `anthropic` SDK (not raw HTTP, not an OpenAI-compatible shim), explicit effort, and the server-side refusal fallback.

<contract_rules>
R1 (MUST NOT): claw-dj runs no OAuth flow and writes no credential, token, or API key anywhere; sign-in belongs to the vendor CLI and keys live only in the user's gitignored `.env` or environment.
R2 (MUST): any failure (not installed, not signed in, missing key, HTTP error, timeout, refusal) raises `ProviderError` with a human-readable reason, never a raw subprocess or HTTP exception.
R3 (MUST): an unknown provider name, including the retired `nemoclaw` and `h-agent`, raises `ProviderError`.
R4 (MUST): `status_all()` never raises and never prompts.
R5 (MUST NOT): a provider being unavailable blocks any caller that can work without a model.
</contract_rules>

% Shared DJ brain providers (2026-10-05)

The provider registry serves curation, DJ-note interpretation and mix planning.
Add `hcompany-api` (label H Company Holo API key), enabled by `HAI_API_KEY`
alone, calling https://api.hcompany.ai/v1/chat/completions with bearer auth.
The configuration example recommends current flagship `holo4-27b` with funded
access; document `holo4-35b-a3b` as the faster Holo4 alternative. Keep the
key-only default free-tier model; never silently upgrade a configured account.
`CLAWDJ_HCOMPANY_MODEL` optionally overrides `holo3-1-35b-a3b` (free-tier
model documented by H); never use hai-agents, cloud environments or desktop
tools for these text calls. Status indicates configuration, not proven account
entitlement or DJ quality. No private credential file outside this repo is read.
Refresh file-owned env values when .env changes without replacing shell-owned
values. Removing a file-owned key disables the provider on the next refresh.
Validate nonempty text responses; malformed responses and local reasoning-only
output become ProviderError. Never include credentials or HTTP response bodies
in status/error messages. Status failures are isolated to the failing provider.

